{"seq":1,"slug":"human-structure-physiology","title":"第一章 人体结构与生理","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/human-structure-physiology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cell-and-tissue","title":"大学基础医学 — 细胞与组织","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/human-structure-physiology/cell-and-tissue","wordCount":1966,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"major-organ-systems","title":"大学基础医学 — 主要器官系统","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/human-structure-physiology/major-organ-systems","wordCount":2085,"readingTime":9},{"seq":3,"slug":"nervous-and-endocrine","title":"大学基础医学 — 神经与内分泌调节","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/human-structure-physiology/nervous-and-endocrine","wordCount":1986,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"第一章-人体结构与生理\">第一章 人体结构与生理</h1><p>本章带你认识人体这台&quot;机器&quot;的硬件与运转方式。我们从最小的生命单位——细胞讲起，看它如何组成组织、器官和系统，再聚焦几个最核心的生理系统，理解它们如何协同维持生命。</p>\n<p>理解结构是理解功能的前提。每一个看似复杂的生理现象（心跳、呼吸、神经传导）背后，都有清晰的结构基础和物理化学规律。本章帮你建立&quot;结构决定功能&quot;的核心思维，为后续学习生化、病理打下地基。</p>\n"}